1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 e5 7. Nb3 Nbd7 { In this chapter, we will start looking at the main line. } 8. g4 { We utilize Black's previous move, and we can clearly see why we chose Nb3. } { [%csl Yb3,Yd7,Gg4] } 8... h6 { The most common reply. It's
a logical measure against g5, but } { [%cal Rg4g5] } (8... d5 { This is Black's best response, and we will analyze it in the next chapter. }) (8... Nc5?? { Just very bad. } { [%csl Rc5] } 9. Nxc5 Bxg4 { Only justification, but it doesn't save anything for Black. } (9... dxc5 { The endgame is
