ideas for Black. }) 10. Bxf4 h6 { Only logical move. } 11. g6! { Strong pawn sacrifice to keep the h8-rook restricted. } { [%csl Bg6,Rh8] } 11... fxg6 12. Qd4 Ngf6 13. O-O-O { Black is far behind in development and suffers a lot. For example } 13... Qb6 14. Qd3 { Of course, we want to keep the
queens. } 14... g5 15. e5! { Going after the king. } { [%csl Be5,Rg6] } 15... gxf4 16. Qg6+ Kd8 17. exf6 Nxf6 18. Bg2 $16 { Black is two pawns up,
but is very passive and has huge problems with the king. } { [%csl Rd8] }) 9. g5 { We can play it anyway. } { [%csl Bg5] } 9... Ng8! { The only good move,
but it was only played once. } { [%csl Bg8] } (9... hxg5? { The most common by far (19/20 games), but this is a serious mistake! } 10. fxg5 Nh5 { Looks fine
