mistake. } 14. Nc5 $18 { White eliminates the dark-squared bishop, and Black is simply lost. } { [%csl Bc5][%cal Gc5e6] }) 14. Bxc4 Bxc4 15. Nd5 Bxd5 16. Rxd5 $16 { White has very easy play and a big advantage. } { [%cal Gc1b1,Gb3c1,Gc1d3,Gh1f1] }) (11... b5 { Typical move. } 12. Be3 Bb7 13. O-O-O Be7 14. h4 $18 { Transposes into the 11...Be7 move order. }) (11... Nf4 { GMs Iljiushenok and Tazbir tried
sacrificing a pawn to get the d7-knight into the game. } { [%cal Gc1f4,Ge5f4,Bd7e5] } 12. h4! { But we can simply ignore this and carry on with
development. } { [%cal Gc1e3,Ge1c1] } 12... f6 { Fedoseev-Iljiushenko, 2020. Fedoseev took now, but even stronger was } 13. g6 $146 { [%csl Bg6] } 13... Nxg6 14. h5 Nf4 15. Be3 $18 { And f6 severely weakened the light squares, so Black is just lost already. We can just play O-O-O
