forcing and testing. } { [%csl Rb5] } (17. Qh4 $13 { Also possible for a complex fight. }) 17... gxf5 18. exf5 d5! { Black must go for a counter
here. } { [%csl Bd5] } 19. Be2 { Dodging e4, and now Black must do something about axb5. } { [%cal Re5e4,Ga4b5] } 19... b4 20. cxb4 Qxc2 { Looks very active, but after } 21. Rf2 { White has everything under control and threatens Bb5+, but Black is fine after } { [%cal Ge2b5] } 21... Bxf5 { [%csl Bf5,Rh3] } 22. Qe3 Qe4 { Most logical, and we can go Qb6 here, but also } { [%cal Ge3b6] } 23. Qxe4 Bxe4 24. b5 $44 { This endgame is very interesting to play for White,
as Black still needs to solve some problems. }) 12... b5 { Black's best. } (12... d5 { Concrete try. } 13. fxg6 Nxg6 14. exd5 Nb6 15. Qg2! { Important move. We don't want to give the pawn back for nothing. } { [%csl Gd5,Bg2] } 15... Bb4 16. Be3 { Black still cannot
