comes and White keeps a huge initiative. } { [%cal Ge4f5] }) 9. Bg2! $146 { Very instructive improvement. } { [%csl Bg2] } 9... Nxe4 (9... dxe4 10. g5 Nh5 11. Nxe4 $16 { Huge issues for Black. } { [%cal Gf5f6,Ge1g1,Rf8g7] }) 10. Ndb5!! { Key tactic. } { [%csl Rc7,Rd5,Re4][%cal Gb5c7,Gc3d5] } 10... axb5 11. Nxd5 Qa5+ (11... Qe5 12. Bf4 $18 { White wins. } { [%csl Re5] }) 12. b4! { Another tempo. } 12... Qd8 13. Bb2!? $18 { Using that Nf6 is impossible,
White wins material. } { [%cal Re4f6,Gd5f6] }) (7... Nbd7 { Logical, but a bit slow. } 8. g4! $146 { White continues in the natural spirit. } { [%csl Gg4][%cal Gg4g5] } 8... b5 { Engine's typical defense. } { [%cal Rg4g5,Gb5b4] } (8... h6 9. Qe2 { Both e6 and g6 are unpleasant to play. } { [%cal Ye7e6,Yg7g6,Gc1d2,Ge1c1] } 9... Ne5 10. g5 hxg5 11. Bxg5 $16 { Same development problems persist, White is much better. } { [%csl Re8,Rf8][%cal Ge1c1] }) 9. Bg2 { We can play for
