strong GMs like Paravyan, Safarli and Lagno. } { [%cal Ge2h5] } 9... Be7 { Black's best. } (9... Nc6?! { Safarli-Weber, 2024. } 10. Nxc6 Qxc6 11. Bg5! $146 { Even stronger than Bh5+ immediately. } { [%cal Ge2h5] } (11. Bh5+?! { less convincing. } 11... Nxh5 12. Qxh5+ g6 { The bishop is
still on f8, so it can go to g7. } { [%csl Gf8][%cal Gf8g7] }) 11... Be7 12. Bh5+! { As usual, since Black's bishop is already on e7. } { [%csl Re7][%cal Rg7g6] } 12... g6 13. Bf3 $16 { Big positional advantage. } { [%csl Rg7,Rh6] }) 10. Bh5+! { White's idea, Black can't fianchetto the bishop anymore. } { [%cal Rf8g7] } 10... g6 (10... Nxh5 { leads to easy play. } 11. Qxh5+ g6 12. Qh6!? $14 { Any square is good. } { [%cal Rc7c5,Gd4f3,Gc1g5] }) 11. Be2 { Now
the dark squares on the kingside are forever weak. } { [%csl Yg7,Yh6] } 11... O-O { Paravyan-Bocharov, 2020. } (11... e5 $146 { Human attempt, to develop with Be6 next. } 12. Nb3 Be6 13. Bh6 { We can stop castling for now. } { [%cal Re8g8] } (13. Nd5!? { also deserves attention. } 13... Bxd5 { Best. } (13... Nxd5?! 14. exd5 Bf5 15. c4 $14 { This should definitely be in White's favor. } { [%csl Rg7,Rh6] }) 14. exd5 Nbd7 15. Qd3 $13 { With a playable
