it's a novelty. } (9... O-O { Logical development. } 10. Qe2! { It's important not to allow Nh5 here. } { [%csl Be2][%cal Rf6h5] } 10... Be6 11. g4 h6 { Logical against g5. } { [%cal Rg4g5] } 12. O-O-O Nbd7 13. Rg1 { We have a simple plan, but } { [%cal Gh3h4,Gg4g5] } 13... Rc8 { we should be
aware of Black's counterplay. } { [%cal Gc8c3] } 14. g5! { Only move for the advantage. } { [%csl Bg5] } 14... hxg5 15. Rxg5 { [%csl Rg7][%cal Ge2g2] } 15... Rxc3! { Only
critical. } 16. bxc3 Qb6 17. Qg2 Ne8 { Only move. } 18. h4! $16 { The most precise, and now White has
a nice positional advantage. } { [%csl Bh4][%cal Gf1e2,Gc1b2,Be7g5,Bh4g5] }) 10. Qd3 { My recommendation. } { [%csl Bd3,Rd6,Ge4] } 10... Bb7 11. O-O-O O-O { Best option. } 12. Bxd6 { It might seem
strange to go into an endgame, but it's very promising for White. } 12... Bxd6 13. Qxd6 Qxd6 14. Rxd6 Nxe4 { Black must recapture immediately. } 15. Nxe4 Bxe4 16. Nc5 Bc6 { A very sad, but necessary move. } 17. Rh2 { Aiming to finish development. } { [%csl Bh2][%cal Gg2g4] } 17... Re8 18. g4 { Black cannot go for a counter here. } { [%csl Rg8][%cal Re8e1] } 18... Kf8 19. Rf2 $14 { With a very promising endgame for White. } { [%csl Ra8,Rb8,Rc6] } *


