1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 g6 { Rare option, but a natural one. Black wants to fianchetto the bishop. } 7. e5!? { The most principled - we aim for a good structure. } { [%csl Be5] } 7... dxe5! { Necessary. } 8. fxe5 { Black has two main moves, which were played
equally thirty times each: } 8... Ng4 { More direct. } (8... Nd5 { More positional. } 9. Qf3!? { My recommendation. } { [%csl Bf3] } 9... Nxc3 10. Qxc3 { White's idea is to keep the structure intact. } { [%csl Gc3] } 10... Bg7 11. Bf4 O-O 12. O-O-O { Starting position. } 12... Qb6 { Zemlyanskii-Nepo, Wch Rapid 2025. } 13. a4!? $146 { Annoying move - let's put Black's queen to the test. } { [%csl Ba4][%cal Ga4a5] } 13... Bg4 { Engine recommendation. } 14. a5 Qd8 15. Rd2 Qc8 16. Qxc8 Rxc8! { Due to our pawn being on a5, this is possible. } 17. h3!? { Still, White can fight for some small edge. } 17... Bd7 18. Bd3 Nc6 19. Nxc6 Bxc6 20. Re1 $14 { Three versus two on the queenside, passive bishop on g7. I can't
say that White will win this 100% of the time, but some practical chances exist. } { [%csl Ga5,Ya6,Gb2,Yb7,Gc2,Rg7][%cal Gd3e4] }) 9. e6! { White's main idea of the line. } { [%csl Ge6] } 9... f5 { Most common move. } (9... Bxe6! { Best, but it's a bit sad. } 10. Nxe6 Qxd1+ 11. Nxd1 fxe6 { Black is a pawn up for now, but that's the only
good news in the position. } 12. Bc4 { Let's attack it. } { [%csl Ye6] } 12... e5 { Only move that has been played. } 13. Ne3!? { If we manage
to exchange the knight, it would be wonderful. } { [%csl Gg4] } 13... Nf6! { Best. } 14. Nd5! $146 { We force it. } { [%csl Gd5] } 14... Nxd5 15. Bxd5 Nc6 16. Be4 $14 { Pair of bishops and three versus two on the queenside lead to a lot of favorable
scenarios long term. } { [%csl Ga2,Ya6,Gb2,Yb7,Bc1,Gc2,Be4][%cal Gc2c3,Gc1e3,Ge1c1] }) 10. h3 { to kick the knight back } 10... Ne5 { Best, to stop Bc4 and support Nbc6 as well. } { [%cal Rf1c4,Gb8c6] } 11. Be3 { The structure is very atypical, but the e6-pawn is an actual strength, making Black's king very vulnerable.
Development-wise, White has more natural moves. } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Gd1d2,Ge1c1] } 11... Nbc6! { Necessary. } { [%csl Gc6] } 12. Nxc6 { Trading queens. } 12... Qxd1+ 13. Rxd1 bxc6 { Necessary, to guard d5. } { [%csl Gd5] } 14. Na4!? { Most annoying. } { [%cal Ba4b6] } 14... Bxe6 15. Nb6 Ra7 $146 { Best for the engine, but a difficult move as it
runs into: } 16. Nc4! { Picking up the exchange. } 16... Nxc4 17. Bxc4 Bxc4 18. Bxa7 e5! 19. Kf2 $14 { It's quite simple
to fix the pawns on dark squares, and later slowly use the d-file to infiltrate. } { [%cal Gh1e1,Re5e4,Gg2g3] } *


