1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 Nbd7!? { The only critical sideline, as it prevents e5 and has
the idea to develop to c5. } { [%cal Ye4e5,Gd7c5] } 7. Be3 { Rare, but most interesting, I believe. } { [%cal Ge1c1] } 7... Nc5 { Black's best attempt, putting
pressure on e4. } { [%csl Re4] } (7... e6 { slow. } 8. g4 h6 9. Qe2 $16 { Dream position - everything is where it should be. } { [%cal Ge1c1,Gf1g2] }) (7... g6!? { Better development try, as g4 is less good. } 8. Be2 { In this case, we can slowly develop. } 8... Bg7 9. Qd2! { Still, our goal is
long castling. } { [%cal Ge1c1] } 9... O-O 10. O-O-O Re8! { Best try, preparing b5. } { [%csl Ge7][%cal Rd4c6,Gb7b5] } 11. Bf3 { Prophylaxis. } 11... Nb6 12. b3 Qc7 13. h3 $14 { White is super safe and can later react accordingly to Black's play. } { [%cal Gc1b1,Gd1c1,Gg2g4] }) 8. Bc4!? $146 { Good
novelty - we want to put pressure on the diagonal and provoke e6. } { [%csl Yf7][%cal Ye7e6] } 8... Bg4! { Black's idea, using that Be2 isn't what we want
now. } { [%cal Yc4e2] } (8... Nfxe4? { falls for our small trap. } 9. Nxe4 Nxe4 10. Qh5 $18 { e6 is not possible. } { [%csl Rf7][%cal Re7e6,Gd4e6] }) 9. Nf3 { h3 is coming, so Black must act. } { [%cal Gh2h3] } 9... b5!? { Most dangerous. } { [%csl Rc4,Ye4] } (9... Nfxe4? { Critical, but bad. } 10. Nxe4 Nxe4 11. Qd5! { Triple attack. } { [%csl Rb7,Re4,Rf7][%cal Gd5f7,Gd5b7,Gd5e4] } 11... e6 12. Qxb7! { Key intermezzo, since Qc6+ is a decisive threat. } { [%cal Bb7c6] } 12... Be7 13. Qc6+ Kf8 14. Qxe4 d5 15. Bxd5 exd5 16. Qd3 $16 { Pawn up - White will slowly convert the material advantage. }) 10. Be2 Nfxe4 { Start
of a forcing line: } 11. Nxe4 Nxe4 12. Ng5! { Key move. } { [%csl Gg5] } 12... Bxe2! { Necessary. } 13. Qd5! { This
was our nasty idea. } { [%csl Re8,Rf7][%cal Gd5f7,Gd5c6] } 13... Bg4!! { Only defense. } { [%csl Bg4] } 14. Qxf7+ Kd7 15. Nxe4 { And here Black must find another incredible defense. } 15... Qc8!! { Strictly the only move. } { [%cal Re4c5] } 16. f5 Qc4! { Another key idea of Qc8. } { [%csl Gc4] } 17. Qxc4 bxc4 18. O-O $14 { The worst part is over for Black, but I wouldn't say that he solved everything. White is still more comfortable in this endgame. } { [%csl Rf8][%cal Ge3d4] } *


